{"qid":"Q1037","names":["Republic of Rwanda"],"title":"Republic of Rwanda","endonym":{"native":"Republic of Rwanda","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Rwanda became a republic on 28 January 1961 following a Hutu-led revolution that abolished the Tutsi monarchy, and gained independence from Belgian trusteeship on 1 July 1962. The country suffered cycles of ethnic violence culminating in the genocide against the Tutsi of April–July 1994, in which an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 people were killed in approximately 100 days before the Rwandan Patriotic Front under Paul Kagame ended the killing in July 1994. Under Kagame's presidency (formally from 2000), Rwanda rebuilt its institutions and achieved sustained economic growth, with GDP per capita rising more than fivefold between 1995 and 2023.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Rwanda's territorial boundaries are precisely defined by international treaty and are uncontested; the attestation window reflects the republican period from 1963 onward.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Rwanda","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Rwanda"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Rwanda","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rwanda"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Rwandan genocide","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rwandan_genocide"}],"britannica":"place/Rwanda","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Rwanda","rulers":[{"qid":"Q557995","name":"Grégoire Kayibanda","start":1961,"end":1973,"image":"1649592763733 19650300 RWANDA 45.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/1649592763733%2019650300%20RWANDA%2045.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Attribution","artist":"© E